course: dictionary
lesson: 15515
title: Subsequently: afterwards or later
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Subsequently» is a formal word meaning afterwards or later. Writers use it in reports, stories and maths problems to show that one thing happened after another.
explain: «She bought 10 sweets and subsequently ate 3.» First she bought the sweets, then, after that, she ate 3. The clue is the order: buying comes first, and eating comes after.
explain: To check, swap in a simpler word. «She bought 10 sweets and then ate 3» means the same thing, so subsequently means then, or later on.
fact: Subsequently means afterwards or later.
fact: «The town was subsequently rebuilt» means the town was rebuilt after something had happened to it.
fact: Subsequently is a formal word, so you will see it more in reports and exams than in everyday talk.
fact: If you are not sure, use «then» or «after that» in your own writing. They mean much the same.
exercise: «Mia finished her spellings and subsequently went out to play.» What does subsequently mean here? | Very loudly | Before her spellings | *Afterwards | Instead of playing
exercise: «The bridge was damaged in the storm and subsequently repaired.» What happened to the bridge after the storm? | *It was repaired later | It was built for the first time | It was never seen again | It was painted red
exercise: «He lost his pencil and subsequently found it in his bag.» Find and copy the word that tells you when he found the pencil. | pencil | *subsequently | bag | lost
test: «The match was paused and subsequently restarted when the rain stopped.» What does subsequently mean? | At the start | Quickly | *Afterwards | Never
test: Which word means the same as subsequently? | *Later | Sadly | Earlier | Before
exam: Mia wrote, «I had lunch and subsequently did my homework.» Which word could replace subsequently without changing the meaning? | Gently | Never | Quietly | *Then
